== Trivia ==
* Round Worms are parasitic creatures in real life that can be found inside cats or dogs.
* Nightcrawlers in real life could refer to earthworms, although they don't look similar to the Nightcrawlers from ''The Binding of Isaac''.
* {{dlc|a}} Ulcers are a reference to [[wikipedia:Ulcer|ulcers]], breaks in bodily membranes caused by sloughing out of inflamed necrotic tissue.
* {{dlc|a+}}Tube Worms were created by Kilburn,<ref>Booster Pack #4 is Live! - [https://www.reddit.com/r/bindingofisaac/comments/75ma1q/booster_pack_4_is_live/ r/bindingofisaac]</ref> who later became the programmer and developer for the ''Repentance'' DLC.
* In real-life, tube worms are creatures that live underwater and anchor their tails underground, which may be where the Tube Worm from ''The Binding of Isaac'' got its name from. However, they don't resemble real-life tube worms.
* {{dlc|r}}The [[Anti:Fireworm|Fireworm]] first appeared in the ''Antibirth'' mod where its name was one word instead of two.

